# The carrier of a road that is taken down walks home west along the first road (docs/rules/settlers.md, "Passing"). The
# woodcutter that meets it head-on on the original's script walked out from the castle to a hut put down by a command; a
# finished hut stands with its worker inside at tick 0 (the layout's finished-building entry), so no woodcutter walks out
# east along the road at that moment, and a hut put down in the run is a building site with no worker. The pass with a
# woodcutter is pinned by the golden scenario head-on-pass-layout (GoldenTests, which puts the finished hut down at tick
# 401) and by HeadOnPassTests. This script keeps the carrier's walk home.
# Run it on the layout: sh tools/play-run.sh head-on-pass --layout layouts/head-on-pass.jsonc --fps 10
wait 32
name cr 16 11 carrier
button Remove
click-tile 15 11
button Remove
wait 1
shot start
# The carrier walks home west along the first road and enters the castle's storage.
fast-forward until ticks >= 1000 max 3000
wait 0.3
expect-event cr stepped cause razed
expect-event cr entered-storage cause razed
events cr carrier
shot walks-home 13 11 2 2
